# Spark DS — Documentation Authoring

Applies when editing pages in this docs repo (`*.html`, `README.md`).

## Writing style

- Practical and brief. Lead with what to use and when.
- Do not use em dashes in documentation prose.
- Do not reference fake stories, placeholder products, or undocumented components as if they ship.

## Page structure (components)

Follow `button.html` as the template:

1. Overview and anatomy
2. Live examples for all variants and states
3. Token tables mapping props/classes to CSS variables
4. Usage guidelines (designers and developers)
5. Accessibility section
6. Spacing and sizing tables

## Tokens in docs

- Every token shown in docs must exist in `css/tokens.css`.
- Explain the 3-tier model: Primitive (raw) → Semantic (meaning) → Component (scoped).
- State clearly that primitives must not be used directly in product UI.

## Code examples

- HTML examples in docs may use class names directly.
- React prop tables must match implementable API (see Button props in `button.html`).
- Do not paste example code that uses hardcoded hex or px where tokens exist.

## Navigation

Add new component pages to the sidebar in every HTML file and to the home grid on `index.html`.
